                <pb facs="0212" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v08/pg190"/>

                <head>95. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On September 10 and 11, Afghan and Pakistani Cabinet Ministers, including Foreign
                    Minister Naim, raised the Pakistani flag at <pb facs="0213" n="191"
                        xml:id="pg191"/> ceremonies in Kabul and Jalalabad. A Pakistani Cabinet
                    Minister then raised the Afghan flag at a ceremony on September 12 at Peshawar.
                    Immediately after these ceremonies, Pakistan and Afghanistan reopened the
                    Consulates and trade agencies.</p>
                <p>The Department of State was pleased that the two nations had amicably settled
                    this protracted dispute. “We believe successful conclusion agreement resulted
                    from statesmanlike and conciliatory efforts of both sides,” it cabled the
                    Embassies at Kabul and Karachi. “We are hopeful new period cordial relations
                    between two countries being commenced.” (Telegram 566 to Karachi, September 10;
                    Department of State, Central Files, 689.90D/9–855)</p>
            </div>
